  "worked_solution": "First, we simplify the phrase \"the bike is green and it is a green bike\" to just \"the bike is green.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The bike is blue or the bike is green, or the bike is green.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:\n\n\"The bike is blue, or the bike is green or the bike is green.\"\n\nNow, we simplify the phrase \"the bike is green or the bike is green\" to just \"the bike is green.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"the bike is blue or the bike is green.\"\n\nFinally, we simplify the sentence to\n\n\"The bike is blue or green.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
