  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-82999\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p></p><p>First, we simplify the phrase \"the bike is green and it is a green bike\" to just \"the bike is green.\" The sentence now reads</p><p></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The bike is blue or the bike is green, or the bike is green.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Then, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The bike is blue, or the bike is green or the bike is green.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Now, we simplify the phrase \"the bike is green or the bike is green\" to just \"the bike is green.\" The sentence now reads</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"the bike is blue or the bike is green.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Finally, we simplify the sentence to</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The bike is blue or green.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n</div>",
